<%# The NFL-season rules page. Sibling of pages/turf_totals_v1 (World Cup), and
    deliberately NOT a copy of it — the two sports price and score differently:

      multiplier   NFL is LINEAR, 1 + (rank-1)/(N-1), topping out at x2.0.
                   The World Cup curve is logarithmic and tops out at x3.0.
                   (SlateMatchup.turf_score_for, sport: "nfl")
      scoring unit NFL counts POINTS SCORED (Goal::SCORING_TYPE_POINTS: TD 6,
                   FG 3, 2-pt 2, safety 2, PAT 1), not goals.
      span         An NFL contest runs on a SPAN slate ("NFL 2026 Weeks 1-3"),
                   so a team plays three games under ONE frozen multiplier and
                   scores its SUMMED points (Selection#compute_points!).

    Every number below is read from the live Weeks 1-3 slate, not invented. The
    WEEKLY point totals in the scoring example are hypothetical results (those
    games have not been played) and the page says so where they appear.

    ENTRY COST LINKS OUT, ALWAYS. Operator rule: this page teaches game play,
    and every mention of what an entry costs sends the reader to
    getting_started_path — the Web3 onboarding guide that owns wallet setup and
    funding. Do not explain USDC purchase here; link to the page that does. %>
<% content_for :title, "Turf Monster v1 — How It Works" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "NFL pick'em: choose 6 teams, score their points across Weeks 1-3 multiplied by their Turf Score, and climb the leaderboard for cash prizes." %>

<%# data-test hook: the tests scope their copy assertions to THIS subtree. The
    surrounding layout ships site-wide meta that still advertises the World Cup
    season, so a page-wide response.body scan would read the chrome, not the
    page. %>
<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-8 px-2" data-test="turf-monster-rules">

  <!-- ========== HERO ========== -->
  <section class="text-center mb-14">
    <div class="mb-4 flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
      <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-primary-900/30 text-primary text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest rounded-full border border-primary-700">NFL 2026</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-heading mb-2">
      Turf <span class="text-primary">Monster</span>
      <span class="ml-2 px-2 py-0.5 bg-violet/20 text-violet text-sm md:text-base font-mono rounded-md align-middle border border-violet/30">v1</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-body mt-4 mb-3">Pick teams. Stack points. Get paid.</p>
    <p class="text-secondary text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto mb-8">
      Choose 6 NFL teams. Every point they score over three weeks counts &mdash; multiplied by that team&rsquo;s Turf Score. Lower-scoring teams carry a bigger multiplier, so a good underdog beats an obvious favorite.
    </p>
    <%= link_to "Start Playing", root_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg shadow-lg shadow-primary/20 text-lg" %>
  </section>

  <!-- ========== HOW TO PLAY — the four steps ========== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-2 text-center">How to play</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-center mb-8">Four steps. That&rsquo;s the whole game.</p>

    <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <li class="card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-primary text-sm">01</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Pick a contest</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Open <%= link_to "Contests", contests_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %> and choose one. Each contest names the weeks it covers, how many players it holds, and the prizes on the line.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-primary text-sm">02</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Choose your teams</h3>
        </div>
        <%# CORRECTED 2026-09-08. This step read "Swap freely until the contest
            locks at the first kickoff", and contradicted section 07 on its own
            page in two ways at once.

            "Swap freely" dropped the qualifier section 07 carries: a team whose
            game has ALREADY kicked off is frozen while the contest is still
            open and its lock still ahead.

            "At the first kickoff" named the wrong moment. Contest.locks_at is
            starts_at, then the slate first kickoff, then the slate start
            (contest.rb lines 686 to 693): an explicit starts_at WINS, it is
            admin-permitted on create AND edit, and nothing validates it against
            the slate. The two moments coincide in TWO ways, not one: when an
            admin leaves starts_at blank, so the derivation falls through to
            that kickoff; and when an admin SETS starts_at to exactly that
            kickoff, which nothing forbids. The second way is the one the World
            Cup rulebook's worked example depicts, at a lock and a first kickoff
            both 3pm. So a comment naming only the blank case loses an argument
            with that example, and a reader who catches a comment in a
            half-truth discards the rest of it. Any OTHER explicit starts_at
            splits the two, and that is the case which makes "at the first
            kickoff" false.

            Both halves now agree with section 07, and
            test/integration/turf_totals_lock_rule_test.rb holds this subtree to
            the SAME two measurements section 07 answers to, so the two cannot
            drift apart again. The data-test hook is what scopes those
            assertions here; without it they read the whole page and pass on
            section 07's copy. %>
        <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed" data-test="nfl-pick-step">
          Tap 6 teams from the board. Each card shows the team&rsquo;s Turf Score and its opponents. Until the contest locks at its stated start time, you can swap any team whose game has not kicked off.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-primary text-sm">03</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Watch the leaderboard</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Every point your teams score is added to your entry, and the contest leaderboard shows where you stand against everyone else.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2">
          <span class="font-mono text-primary text-sm">04</span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Win prizes</h3>
        </div>
        <%# NO TIMING PROMISE HERE, DELIBERATELY. An earlier draft of this card
            said "no withdrawal request, no waiting on a payout queue" and all
            three timing claims were false: nothing grades at the final whistle
            (Contest#grade! is reached only from the admin controller and the QA
            rehearsal driver — no cron in config/schedule.yml grades or settles),
            and settlement IS a queue (Contest#settle_onchain! builds a
            PARTIALLY-SIGNED transaction into PendingTransaction for 2-of-3
            multisig cosigning, which an admin confirms; production was holding
            settle pt#298 for two days when this was caught in review).
            WHERE the money goes is true and is all this may claim: settle_onchain!
            pays entry.user.solana_address. Nobody here knows the payout SLA, so
            the page states none — do not reintroduce one without a measured
            number and an owner. Guarded by pages_controller_test. %>
        <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
          When the last game is over the standings are final, and payouts go to the wallet you entered from.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="text-muted text-sm text-center mt-6">
      Entries are paid in USDC. New to that? The
      <%= link_to "Getting Started guide", getting_started_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>
      walks you through a wallet and funding it, start to finish.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 01 — THE BASICS ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">01</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">The Basics</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      You are picking a team to put points on the board, not to win. Nobody has to beat anybody &mdash; a team that loses 38&ndash;35 scored 35 points, and every one of them counts for you. It is the scoreboard that counts, so a defensive or special-teams touchdown pays you exactly like any other. A contest that covers Weeks 1&ndash;3 counts all three of that team&rsquo;s games.
    </p>

    <%# The SAME card the board draws, minus the tap target — team gradient,
        city over mascot in the team accent, the span multiplier, and the three
        opponents each in their own brand colour. %>
    <div class="max-w-xs mx-auto">
      <%= render "pages/rules_team_card", example: TurfMonsterRules::FEATURE, teams: @teams %>
      <p class="text-center text-muted text-xs mt-3 italic">A real card from the Weeks 1&ndash;3 board &mdash; three opponents, one multiplier</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 02 — YOUR ENTRY ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">02</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">Your Entry</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      An entry is <span class="text-heading font-semibold">6 teams</span>. Pick them from the board, then hold to confirm. You can enter the same contest up to 3 times with different lineups.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-2xl border border-subtle p-4 sm:p-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
        <% TurfMonsterRules::LINEUP.each do |example| %>
          <%= render "pages/rules_team_card", example: example, teams: @teams, compact: true %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="text-muted text-sm text-center mt-4">
        Six real teams from the Weeks 1&ndash;3 board, favorites through longshots.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 03 — TURF SCORE ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">03</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">Turf Score</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      All 32 teams are ranked by how many points they are projected to score across the contest&rsquo;s weeks. Rank 1 is the highest projection and prices at <span class="text-violet font-mono font-bold">1.0&times;</span>; rank 32 prices at <span class="text-violet font-mono font-bold">2.0&times;</span>. In between, a rank is worth <span class="text-violet font-mono font-bold">1 + (rank &minus; 1) / 31, rounded to one decimal</span> &mdash; NFL scoring runs close to linear. The rounding is not a detail: it is the number that gets frozen onto your pick and paid, so ranks 1 and 2 both price at <span class="text-violet font-mono font-bold">1.0&times;</span>, and ranks 3, 4 and 5 all price at <span class="text-violet font-mono font-bold">1.1&times;</span>. Your points are <span class="text-heading font-semibold">points scored &times; Turf Score</span>.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-3 mb-6">
      <% TurfMonsterRules::CURVE.each do |row| %>
        <% team = @teams[row[:team_slug]] %>
        <div class="rounded-xl p-5 text-center bg-surface-alt border border-subtle">
          <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-1">Rank #<%= row[:rank] %> &mdash; <%= team&.mascot || row[:team_slug].titleize %></p>
          <%# One decimal, like every other multiplier on this page: these three
              cards show a RANGE, and "1x / 1.5x / 2x" reads as three unrelated
              numbers where "1.0x / 1.5x / 2.0x" reads as a scale. %>
          <p class="text-3xl font-mono font-bold text-violet mb-1"><%= number_with_precision(TurfMonsterRules.turf_score_for_rank(row[:rank]), precision: 1) %>&times;</p>
          <p class="text-secondary text-xs"><%= row[:note] %></p>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl border border-violet/30 p-6">
      <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-3">What counts as a point</p>
      <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The scoreboard does. Touchdown 6, field goal 3, extra point 1, two-point conversion 2, safety 2 &mdash; a team&rsquo;s final score is what you are credited with, and a defensive or special-teams touchdown counts the same as any other.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 04 — SCORING EXAMPLE ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">04</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">Scoring Example</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      <%# Every number AND both team names come from TurfMonsterRules.comparison.
          The hand-written version pointed at "the bottom two rows" while naming
          the first and fifth, so a reader who followed it compared the wrong
          pair. Derived, the sentence cannot drift from the table under it.
          "hypothetical" is load-bearing: these weekly results are invented, and
          saying so in the lead beats a disclaimer under the table. %>
      <% c = TurfMonsterRules.comparison %>
      <% favorite = @teams[c.favorite.team_slug] %>
      <% longshot = @teams[c.longshot.team_slug] %>
      Here is that same lineup after three <span class="text-heading font-semibold">hypothetical</span> weeks.
      <%= longshot&.location || c.longshot.team_slug.titleize %> put up <%= c.fewer_points %> fewer points than
      <%= favorite&.location || c.favorite.team_slug.titleize %> and still finished <%= number_with_precision(c.points_ahead, precision: 1) %> ahead
      &mdash; <%= number_with_precision(c.longshot.turf_score, precision: 1) %>&times; against <%= number_with_precision(c.favorite.turf_score, precision: 1) %>&times;.
      That is the whole strategy.
    </p>

    <div class="card overflow-x-auto">
      <%# data-test hook: pages_controller_test re-derives every row (weekly points
          summed, times the Turf Score) so the example can never quietly go wrong. %>
      <table class="w-full text-sm min-w-[34rem]" data-test="scoring-example">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-subtle">
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Team</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Wk 1</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Wk 2</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Wk 3</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Turf</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Points</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-subtle">
          <% TurfMonsterRules::LINEUP.each do |example| %>
            <% team = @teams[example.team_slug] %>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-body whitespace-nowrap"><%= team&.emoji %> <%= team&.mascot || example.team_slug.titleize %></td>
              <% example.weekly_points.each do |points| %>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-heading"><%= points %></td>
              <% end %>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center font-mono text-violet"><%= number_with_precision(example.turf_score, precision: 1) %>&times;</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-primary font-bold"><%= number_with_precision(example.entry_points, precision: 1) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <tr class="border-t-2 border-violet/30 bg-surface-alt">
            <td colspan="5" class="px-4 py-3 text-right text-heading font-semibold">Total Score</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-xl text-violet font-bold"><%= number_with_precision(TurfMonsterRules.lineup_total, precision: 1) %></td>
          </tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-secondary text-sm mt-3">
      The teams and Turf Scores are real, read from the Weeks 1&ndash;3 board. The weekly point totals are invented &mdash; those games have not been played.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 05 — LEADERBOARD ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">05</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">The Leaderboard</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      You do not have to wait for the last whistle to find out how you did. As scores come in your entry is re-scored, and the contest page shows where every entry stands and which of your six teams is carrying you.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl border border-violet/30 p-6">
      <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-3">Over three weeks</p>
      <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
        A Weeks 1&ndash;3 contest is a marathon, not a Sunday. A team that gets shut out in Week 1 has two more games to make it back, and the leaderboard rarely settles until the last one is over.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 06 — PRIZES ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">06</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">Prizes</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Every contest posts its prizes before anyone enters, and the pool is funded up front rather than skimmed from the entry fees. The live Weeks 1&ndash;3 contest holds <%= TurfMonsterRules.example_max_entries %> entries and pays the top <%= TurfMonsterRules.example_payouts.size %>: <%= number_to_currency(TurfMonsterRules.example_payouts.first.last, precision: 0) %> for first, <%= number_to_currency(TurfMonsterRules.example_payouts.last.last, precision: 0) %> for second. Tied entries split the prizes for the places they cover, so a two-way tie for first splits first and second money down the middle.
    </p>

    <%# Places and amounts from Contest::FORMATS[medium] — the same table
        Contest#payouts grades against — so a payout change in the app reaches
        this page in the same commit. Review found these hard-typed while the
        multipliers were derived. %>
    <div class="card overflow-hidden mb-6">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-subtle">
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Place</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 text-right text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Payout</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-subtle">
          <% TurfMonsterRules.example_payouts.each_with_index do |(place, dollars), index| %>
            <tr class="<%= "border-l-4 border-l-mint" if index.zero? %>">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 <%= index.zero? ? "text-heading font-semibold" : "text-body" %>"><%= place.ordinalize %> Place</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono <%= index.zero? ? "text-primary font-bold text-lg" : "text-heading" %>"><%= number_to_currency(dollars) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <tr class="border-t-2 border-violet/30 bg-surface-alt">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-heading font-semibold">Total prizes</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-right font-mono text-primary font-bold"><%= number_to_currency(TurfMonsterRules.example_prize_pool) %></td>
          </tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl border border-subtle p-6">
      <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-2">What an entry costs</p>
      <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Entries are paid in USDC, a digital dollar, from a wallet you control. The
        <%= link_to "Getting Started guide", getting_started_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>
        covers all of it &mdash; setting up a wallet, funding it, and confirming your first entry. Prizes are paid back to that same wallet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <%# data-test hook. The pre-lock swap sentence below is pinned by
      test/integration/turf_totals_lock_rule_test.rb, which does not grep for a
      wording: it MEASURES what Entry accepts on a contest whose stated start
      trails a kickoff on its slate, then requires this copy to agree. The
      measurement lives in the World Cup file because Contest and Entry are
      sport-agnostic, so one measurement certifies both rulebooks.

      The hook scopes that assertion to THIS section. Without it the assertion
      reads the site-wide layout too and can pass on chrome. %>
  <!-- ========== 07 — WHEN PICKS LOCK ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16" data-test="lock-rules">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">07</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">When Picks Lock</h2>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
      A contest locks at its stated start time. Until then you can swap any team whose game has not kicked off. After it, the lineup is set for all three weeks; there are no waiver moves and no mid-contest substitutions.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl border border-violet/30 p-6">
      <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-3">Why it locks all at once</p>
      <p class="text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Everyone picks blind, from the same board, before a single snap. Nobody gets to watch Thursday night and then choose Sunday&rsquo;s teams.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== 08 — QUICK REFERENCE ========== -->
  <section class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
    <p class="text-primary font-mono text-sm mb-2">08</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-4">Quick Reference</h2>

    <%# TWO BANDS, LABELLED. Review's finding: this section reprinted ONE
        contest's configuration with no qualifier, in the part of the page a
        reader skims for THE RULES — and Contest::FORMATS carries five other live
        formats with different sizes and payouts. The rules that hold for every
        NFL contest are separated from the numbers that belong to this one, and
        the second band's money is derived from FORMATS rather than typed. %>
    <div class="card border-2 border-violet/50 p-6 shadow-lg shadow-violet/10">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Every NFL contest</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-y-4 gap-x-6 text-sm">
        <div class="text-secondary">Picks per entry</div>
        <div class="font-mono text-heading text-right">6 teams</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Scoring</div>
        <div class="text-right text-heading">Points &times; Turf Score</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Games per team</div>
        <div class="text-right text-heading">All 3 (Weeks 1&ndash;3)</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Turf Score range</div>
        <div class="font-mono text-violet text-right">1.0&times; &ndash; 2.0&times;</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Turf Score formula</div>
        <div class="font-mono text-violet text-right">1 + (rank &minus; 1) / 31, to 1 dp</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Entries per user</div>
        <div class="text-heading text-right">Up to 3</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Ties</div>
        <div class="text-heading text-right">Split the places covered</div>

        <%# This row sits in the EVERY NFL CONTEST band, so it states a rule,
            not one contest's configuration. It read "First kickoff, Week 1",
            which is the same false equivalence corrected in section 02 above
            and is strictly worse here for being claimed as universal: an
            explicit starts_at wins over the slate unvalidated. Hooked and held
            to the measured lock moment. %>
        <div class="text-secondary">Lock</div>
        <div class="text-heading text-right" data-test="nfl-lock-quick-ref">Stated start time</div>

        <div class="text-secondary">Entry</div>
        <div class="text-right"><%= link_to "USDC — see Getting Started", getting_started_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %></div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-subtle mt-6 pt-5">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-muted uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">This contest only</p>
        <p class="text-secondary text-xs mb-3">The live Weeks 1&ndash;3 contest. Other contests set their own size and prizes &mdash; each one states them on its own page.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-y-4 gap-x-6 text-sm">
          <% TurfMonsterRules.example_payouts.each do |place, dollars| %>
            <div class="text-secondary"><%= place.ordinalize %> place</div>
            <div class="font-mono <%= place == 1 ? "text-primary font-bold" : "text-heading" %> text-right"><%= number_to_currency(dollars) %></div>
          <% end %>

          <div class="text-secondary">Total prizes</div>
          <div class="font-mono text-primary font-bold text-right"><%= number_to_currency(TurfMonsterRules.example_prize_pool) %></div>

          <div class="text-secondary">Contest size</div>
          <div class="font-mono text-heading text-right"><%= TurfMonsterRules.example_max_entries %> entries</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-subtle my-10">

  <!-- ========== FOOTER CTA ========== -->
  <section class="text-center py-8">
    <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-heading mb-6">Ready to play?</p>
    <%= link_to "Start Playing", root_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg shadow-lg shadow-primary/20 text-lg" %>
    <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-6">
      Never used a crypto wallet? Start with the
      <%= link_to "Getting Started guide", getting_started_path, class: "text-primary hover:underline" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>
